# OpenDC-LCA Applied Energy CAS submission package

This package uses the supplied Elsevier CAS single-column template
(`cas-sc.cls`, 2024-05-04). Select `main.tex` as the main document in Overleaf
and compile with XeLaTeX. The manuscript and supplementary-information text use
Times New Roman; figure artwork retains its own embedded typography.

The package is deliberately flat. Every source, figure, and data file sits at
the ZIP root, with no subfolders, to satisfy Elsevier Editorial Manager's
requirement for LaTeX submissions.

## Documents

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `main.tex` | Manuscript. Main document for Overleaf and Editorial Manager. |
| `supplement.tex` | Supplementary Information. Compiles independently. |
| `highlights.tex` | Separate upload item. |
| `cover_letter_draft.tex` | Author-facing working file. Carried in the archive, not an Editorial Manager upload item. |
| `SUBMISSION_ACTIONS.md` | Author-facing checklist of open pre-submission actions. Carried in the archive, not an Editorial Manager upload item. |
| `cas-sc.cls`, `cas-common.sty`, `cas-model2-names.bst`, `cas-email.jpeg` | Elsevier CAS template files, unmodified. |

