File names carry their original generation order and do not track figure
numbers. Figures 2--5 are vector PDFs rebuilt from the derived tables by
`scripts/build_applied_energy_figures.py` in the repository.

## Data files

Every derived table named in `main.tex` or `supplement.tex` is included at the
ZIP root, so the evidence manifest in the Supplementary Information resolves
inside the package. Three further derived tables are carried for reviewer
traceability although no sentence cites them by name:
`table19_server_inventory_stress_test.csv`, `table20_method_comparison.csv`,
and `table35_transferability_evidence_map.csv`.

The complete derived-table set, the analysis code, and the provenance manifest
are in the repository and in the DOI-bearing archive named in the manuscript's
data and code availability statement.

## Rebuilding the archive

`scripts/package_applied_energy_cas.py` in the repository writes
`paper/OpenDC-LCA_Applied_Energy_CAS_Overleaf.zip`. It resolves the figure and
data dependencies from the `.tex` sources, fails if any named file is absent,
and ships only declared files, so local build output (`.aux`, `.log`, `.pdf`,
`.xdv`, and similar) never enters the archive.
